19. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Security is mandatory for every new feature.

Review the existing security modules and reuse them where appropriate.

Preserve existing SSRF validation, input sanitization, authentication verification, and error-handling protections.

Do not weaken security controls to make implementation easier.

Required protections

- Authentication verification.
- Authorization checks.
- Input validation.
- Output sanitization.
- Rate limiting where appropriate.
- Safe public identifiers.
- Ownership validation.
- Safe file handling.
- No secret leakage.
- No arbitrary HTML execution.
- Appropriate error handling.
- No sensitive information in public URLs.
- Protection against duplicate reward claims.
- Protection against unauthorized publication.
- Protection against cross-user access.

Do not return raw stack traces or sensitive internal details to users.

Avoid logging private conversation contents or uploaded document text.

Inspect dependency vulnerabilities where supported.

Do not blindly upgrade major dependencies if doing so risks breaking the existing application.

